# TypeScript

- Strict mode is on — no `any`; prefer unknown + narrowing.
- Export named types from `@/types` for shared domain models.
- Prefer `as const` for static config objects; derive types with `typeof` when useful.
- Use zod schemas in `src/lib/validation` for runtime form input; infer types with `z.infer`.
- Prefer explicit return types on public lib helpers.
- Avoid default exports except where Next.js requires them (pages, layouts, configs).
